struct CPS1config is defined in both cps1.h and cps2.h, but the cps2.h copy
lacks the trailing bootleg_kludge field. Under LTO, GCC reports the two
layouts as a One Definition Rule violation, which is fatal with -Werror=odr.
Add the field so both definitions are identical. cps2 initialises the
struct positionally with fewer entries, so the new field keeps its default.

--- a/src/hbmame/includes/cps2.h
+++ b/src/hbmame/includes/cps2.h
@@ -98,2 +98,4 @@
-	int out2_addr = 0;
+	int out2_addr = 0;
+
+	int bootleg_kludge = 0;
 };
